<section id="diagnostic"><div class="shell">
  <div class="shead rv">
    <div class="lbl">The diagnostic</div>
    <h2>Every program begins with a real test.</h2>
    <p>A full-length, timed, adaptive SAT taken at home. What comes back is not a score &mdash; it is a report that separates what your student doesn&rsquo;t know from what the clock took from them, because those need completely different fixes.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="dxwrap rv d1">
    <div class="dxcard">
      <div class="dxhead">
        <span class="dxt">SAT Diagnostic Report</span>
        <span class="dxd">Sample</span>
      </div>
      <div class="dxscore">
        <div>
          <div class="dxbig">1450</div>
          <div class="dxrange">most likely <b>1410&ndash;1490</b> on test day</div>
        </div>
        <div class="dxsplit">
          <div><span class="dxn">730</span><span class="dxl">Reading &amp; Writing</span></div>
          <div><span class="dxn">720</span><span class="dxl">Math</span></div>
          <div><span class="dxn">92%</span><span class="dxl">Accuracy</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="dxwhy">
        <div class="dxwhy-h">Why each question was missed</div>
        <div class="dxbar">
          <i class="w1" style="flex:5"><span>5</span></i>
          <i class="w2" style="flex:2"><span>2</span></i>
          <i class="w3" style="flex:1"><span>1</span></i>
        </div>
        <div class="dxkey">
          <span><i class="w1"></i>Didn&rsquo;t know it &mdash; re-teach the skill</span>
          <span><i class="w2"></i>Took too long &mdash; drill pacing</span>
          <span><i class="w3"></i>Ran out of clock &mdash; fix the strategy</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="dxfoot">Same wrong answer, three different fixes. Most prep guesses at which.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="dxread">
      <div class="dxr"><span class="dxi">1</span><div><h3>A range, not a guess</h3><p>Every score comes with the band it actually sits in. Precision you can trust beats a number that only sounds confident.</p></div></div>
      <div class="dxr"><span class="dxi">2</span><div><h3>Skills ranked by points recoverable</h3><p>So week one starts on the thing that moves the score most &mdash; not on whatever comes first in a textbook.</p></div></div>
      <div class="dxr"><span class="dxi">3</span><div><h3>Where the time actually went</h3><p>Question by question, including minutes spent revisiting questions already answered. Second-guessing is a habit, and it is faster to fix than a knowledge gap.</p></div></div>
      <div class="dxr"><span class="dxi">4</span><div><h3>Honest about small samples</h3><p>Skills seen only once or twice are flagged as unsettled rather than judged. A second sitting resolves them.</p></div></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section id="programs"><div class="shell">
  <div class="shead rv">
    <div class="lbl">What we teach</div>
    <h2>Three programs. One method behind all of them.</h2>
    <p>A real diagnostic, an individualized plan, and a guarantee tied to the outcome &mdash; whether the goal is a score, a grade, or an acceptance.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="offers">
    <a class="offer rv d1" href="prep-course.html">
      <div class="ph"><img src="photo-1-web.jpg" alt="Online SAT tutoring session" loading="lazy"></div>
      <div class="in">
        <div class="k">College Entrance Exams</div>
        <h3>The 12-Week SAT Program</h3>
        <p>Twelve weekly one-on-one sessions built from your student&rsquo;s diagnostic, with full-length timed testing, weekly office hours, and a written update to you every week.</p>
        <div class="cov">SAT &middot; PSAT &middot; AP &amp; IB exams &middot; test-day strategy</div>
        <span class="go">Explore the program &rarr;</span>
      </div>
    </a>
    <a class="offer rv d2" href="math-program.html">
      <div class="ph"><img src="photo-3-web.jpg" alt="In-person math tutoring session" loading="lazy"></div>
      <div class="in">
        <div class="k">Mathematics</div>
        <h3>The Math Mastery Program</h3>
        <p>Not homework help. A diagnostic-driven curriculum built around your student&rsquo;s actual course and textbook, with support between sessions and a guarantee tied to the grade.</p>
        <div class="cov">Algebra 1 &middot; Geometry &middot; Algebra 2 &middot; Precalculus &middot; AP Calculus AB &amp; BC &middot; AP Statistics &middot; Multivariable Calculus &middot; IB Mathematics</div>
        <span class="go">Explore the program &rarr;</span>
      </div>
    </a>
    <a class="offer rv d3" href="applications.html">
      <div class="ph"><img src="photo-2-web.jpg" alt="College application essay coaching" loading="lazy"></div>
      <div class="in">
        <div class="k">College Admissions</div>
        <h3>Essays &amp; Applications</h3>
        <p>One-on-one coaching for the personal statement and every supplemental &mdash; brainstorming, structure, and real revision. Your student writes every word; we make sure every word earns its place.</p>
        <div class="cov">Personal statement &middot; supplementals for every school &middot; deadline tracking &middot; rolling enrollment</div>
        <span class="go">Explore the program &rarr;</span>
      </div>
    </a>
  </div>
</div></section>



<section id="instructor"><div class="shell">
  <div class="instr">
    <div class="pic rv"><img src="Portrait.jpg" alt="Luca Moretti" loading="lazy"></div>
    <div class="rv d1">
      <div class="lbl">Your instructor</div>
      <h2 style="font-family:var(--display);font-size:clamp(1.55rem,2.9vw,2.2rem);margin-top:.65rem;line-height:1.16">Luca Moretti &mdash; founder, and the person who teaches every session.</h2>
      <p style="margin-top:1.15rem;font-size:.96rem;max-width:56ch">Generic tutoring explains tonight&rsquo;s assignment and expires the moment the hour ends. Every plan here starts with a real diagnostic, adapts as a student improves, and is backed by a private portal &mdash; adaptive practice, a weak-spot tracker, and a running log of every missed question &mdash; so we are always working on exactly what is costing points.</p>
      <div class="creds">
        <span>Northwestern University, B.A. Statistics &mdash; in three years</span>
        <span>Dean&rsquo;s List</span>
        <span>1500+ SAT</span>
        <span>5 on AP Calculus AB &amp; BC</span>
        <span>IB Diploma</span>
        <span>Listed with Summit Public Schools</span>
      </div>
      <div class="gbox">
        <div class="k">The guarantee</div>
        <h3>If the score doesn&rsquo;t improve, we keep teaching. Free.</h3>
        <p>Complete the program &mdash; every session and the assigned homework &mdash; and if your student&rsquo;s official score doesn&rsquo;t improve from their diagnostic baseline, we keep working at no additional charge until it does. No family is asked to keep paying for a result that hasn&rsquo;t arrived.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div></section>

